        "response": [
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I found Microsoft documentation about checking whether products are in stock, but not a specific product list or live stock status for your store/site. The docs say you can check **on-hand inventory** for a specific item number in **Inventory management > Inquiries and reports > On-hand list**, and **physical on-hand inventory** in **Warehouse management > Inquiries and reports > Physical on-hand inventory**. [ref_id:0]\n\nThe same documentation also says Commerce can show inventory messages like **“In stock”** or **“Only a few are left,”** and that inventory settings can classify products as **in stock**, **low stock**, or **out of stock**. [ref_id:1] [ref_id:2]\n\nIf you want, I can help you interpret the inventory-check steps for a specific product or store."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
